# Changelog

## [0.10.2] - 2026-11-27

Test tooling and application file organization cleanup.

### Added

- Mockery configuration and a `make mocks` target for regenerating application service, PostgreSQL database, and pgx test mocks.
- Generated Testify mocks and focused terms-acceptance repository unit tests.

### Changed

- Standardize assertions across application, platform, and third-party tests on Testify; promote Testify v1.11.1 to a direct dependency.
- Replace handwritten application service and transactor test doubles with generated mocks and update repository and integration test assertions.
- Rename application use-case implementations and tests to `*_service.go` and `*_service_test.go`.
- Rename the Main BE Temporal startup adapter and its tests from `startup` to `temporal_client`.
- Consolidate workflow startup error definitions in the application service errors file.
- Document mock generation and advance VERSION to 0.10.2.

### Verification

- Release documentation updated from the working tree; tests have not been rerun for this documentation update. CI verification and human review remain outstanding.

## [0.10.1] - 2026-11-27

Application module structure and transaction ownership refactor.

### Changed

- Replace the shared application service with StartApplicationService, AcceptTermsService, and SubmitIdentityService, each with consumer-owned repository interfaces.
- Organize implemented ConnectRPC methods and their narrow service interfaces in use-case files while retaining one Handler and constructor.
- Consolidate identity and terms persistence under ApplicationRepository, with separate application_identity_repository.go and application_terms_acceptance_repository.go implementation files.
- Move AcceptTerms and SubmitIdentity orchestration and transaction boundaries into services through the database-independent Transactor.WithinTx(ctx, fn) contract.
- Centralize PostgreSQL transaction lifecycle management, context binding, cancellation-safe rollback cleanup, and database error mapping; all operations reuse the existing pool.
- Update dependency injection, handwritten stubs, fixtures, and test organization for the focused services and aggregate repository.
- Preserve domain rules, SQL, row locking, atomic status changes, durable replay, error mappings, and Temporal startup after successful identity commit.
- Document the refactored architecture and advance VERSION to 0.10.1.

### Added

- Transactor and service tests for operation order, begin/commit/callback failures, panic rollback, cancellation-safe cleanup, shared transaction contexts, and concurrent context isolation.
- PostgreSQL integration tests proving identity and terms inserts roll back when application status updates fail.
- Makefile test-coverage and coverage-html targets; ignore the generated coverage.out profile.

### Removed

- Obsolete shared application service abstractions.
- Placeholder TestOnboardingWaitsDurablyUntilCanceled test; live Temporal startup integration coverage remains.

### Implementation Status

- Go tests, PostgreSQL integration tests, go vet, and builds passed during the refactor. Local race verification remains blocked by the installed C compiler lacking 64-bit support.
- No protobuf, generated-code, schema, migration, dependency, or runtime workflow behavior changes. CI verification and final human review remain outstanding.

## [0.10.0] - 2026-11-25

Third-party VerifyIdentity API (PR 07).

### Added

- VerifyIdentity through the generated ConnectRPC handler, transport-independent service/domain, and an injected mock provider.
- Structural identity validation preserving submitted values; age and current expiry eligibility remain Main BE responsibilities.
- Seven deterministic synthetic identity records, matched exactly by ID number, full name, birth date, and ID expiry; contact fields do not affect verification.
- Business mismatches return `verified=false`; validation, cancellation, deadlines, provider unavailability, and unexpected failures return distinct sanitized RPC errors.
- Concise domain, service, and mock tests plus a gRPC-over-HTTP/2 integration test covering success, rejection, invalid input, technical errors, and unimplemented sanctions screening.

### Changed

- Third-party server on port 8081 accepts unencrypted HTTP/2 (h2c) using the standard library, with a five-second read-header timeout. HTTP/1 is not enabled.
- Document verification rules, mock fixtures, gRPC/Postman setup, and HTTP/2 health checks; ignore local VS Code configuration.
- VERSION advances to 0.10.0.

### Implementation Status

- No protobuf, generated-code, dependency, database, or workflow changes. Sanctions screening, Temporal Activities, account creation, and result orchestration remain deferred.
- Local Go tests and go vet passed during implementation; race verification remains blocked by the installed C compiler lacking 64-bit support. CI verification and final human review remain outstanding.

## [0.9.0] - 2026-11-24

Temporal workflow startup (PR 06).

### Added

- Injected Temporal startup adapter for SubmitIdentity, called after identity persistence and using the stored application ID as workflow ID.
- REJECT_DUPLICATE and USE_EXISTING policies with duplicate errors preserved for closed-execution classification; start and describe share a three-second request-derived budget without an application retry loop.
- Conditional, parent-row-locked startup status updates that preserve concurrent application progress, plus reconciliation of completed executions against persisted application state.
- Safe client retries after uncertain startup or post-start database failure, preserving identity data; sanitized API errors for unavailable startup and workflow reconciliation failures.
- Local worker registering a minimal deterministic workflow that waits durably without business activities, with graceful shutdown and shared bank-onboarding task queue configuration.
- Focused startup, idempotency, failure recovery, conditional transition, concurrency, and durable-wait tests.

### Changed

- Main BE connects to Temporal through dependency injection with a ten-second connection deadline and managed client lifecycle.
- Pin Temporal Go SDK v1.51.0 and API v1.64.3; align transitive dependencies, including genproto modules.
- Update existing service constructors and identity integration tests for post-persistence startup behavior while retaining identity validation and replay guarantees.
- Document local Temporal configuration, worker startup, error handling, retention limits, and deferred recovery behavior.
- VERSION advances to 0.9.0.

### Implementation Status

- Go tests, including live PostgreSQL integration tests, and go vet passed during implementation. Local race verification remains blocked by the installed C compiler lacking 64-bit support.
- Live Temporal startup and worker-restart smoke tests, CI verification, and final human review remain outstanding.
- No protobuf, generated-code, schema, or migration changes. Business activities, sanctions screening, account creation, human review, and recovery scanners remain deferred.

## [0.8.0] - 2026-11-24

SubmitIdentity validation and persistence (PR 05).

### Added

- SubmitIdentity through ConnectRPC, service, domain rules, and PostgreSQL, validating application UUIDs, required identity fields, 12-digit ID numbers, calendar dates, adult age, and ID expiry using UTC dates.
- Atomic identity insertion and transition from PENDING_IDENTITY_SUBMISSION to PENDING_WORKFLOW_START, serialized by an application-row lock.
- Exact identity replay without writes at progressed states, including after later expiry; changed submissions and invalid states are rejected. Responses return persisted application status and database errors are sanitized.
- Optional email presence is preserved: absent and present empty email remain distinct.
- Pure domain tests, concise service tests, and focused ConnectRPC-to-PostgreSQL tests for persistence, replay, conflicts, invalid states, concurrent submissions, and error mappings.

### Changed

- Terms-related domain errors now live alongside terms acceptance logic, matching identity error organization.
- API, database, sequence, and README documentation describe submission behavior and explicitly defer workflow startup to PR 06.
- VERSION advances to 0.8.0.

### Implementation Status

- No protobuf, generated-code, schema, migration, or dependency changes. Temporal clients, workflow startup, workers, activities, and recovery scanners remain outside PR 05.
- Full Go tests, live PostgreSQL integration tests, and go vet passed during implementation; subsequent constructor simplification passed the full Go suite, and domain error relocation passed domain tests.
- Local race verification remains blocked by GCC lacking 64-bit support; CI verification and final human review remain outstanding.

## [0.7.0] - 2026-11-23

AcceptTerms API with atomic persistence and safe retries (PR 04).

### Added

- AcceptTerms through ConnectRPC, service, domain rules, and PostgreSQL, validating non-nil application UUIDs and nonblank, NUL-free term IDs while preserving exact term values.
- Atomic terms acceptance and transition from PENDING_TERMS_ACCEPTANCE to PENDING_IDENTITY_SUBMISSION, using a transaction and application-row lock to serialize concurrent requests.
- Same-term replay without changing persisted data at later states; conflicting terms and invalid transitions return distinct ConnectRPC errors.
- Table-driven domain tests, concise service validation/error tests, and PostgreSQL/ConnectRPC integration tests for acceptance, replay, errors, and concurrent same-term/different-term requests.

### Changed

- Repository interface is owned by the consuming service package; removed the duplicate repository interface and its empty test file.
- Shared error declarations are organized in errors.go files within domain, service, and repository packages.
- API/database documentation clarifies the one-distinct-term restriction for this flow while preserving the existing one-to-many schema.
- VERSION advances to 0.7.0; README reflects implemented APIs and test coverage.

### Implementation Status

- Protobuf contracts, generated code, migrations, dependencies, and Temporal integration are unchanged.
- Full Go tests, focused PostgreSQL integration tests, and go vet passed during implementation. Subsequent organizational refactors passed non-integration checks and focused domain/service tests; database integration tests were not rerun after those refactors.
- Local race verification remains blocked by a C compiler without 64-bit support; CI and final human review remain outstanding.

## [0.6.0] - 2026-11-22

StartApplication API with durable idempotency (PR 03).

### Added

- StartApplication service and ConnectRPC handler using the existing Application domain and PostgreSQL repository.
- Non-nil request UUID validation and insert-first idempotency: duplicate request IDs return the persisted application ID and current status without overwriting data.
- ConnectRPC error mapping for validation, cancellation, deadlines, and internal failures, with safe client-facing messages.
- Service unit tests for validation, creation, replay, and error propagation; one ConnectRPC-to-PostgreSQL integration test for creation, persistence, replay, and invalid input.
- Optional `.env` loader with environment-variable precedence, safe errors, and unit tests.

### Changed

- Application startup wires the repository, service, and handler; opens PostgreSQL with a startup timeout and closes the pool after graceful HTTP shutdown.
- Application startup and PostgreSQL integration tests load local `.env` configuration automatically; missing files are allowed.
- Environment example includes DATABASE_URL and TEST_DATABASE_URL; README and API/database notes describe the implemented behavior.
- VERSION advances to 0.6.0.

### Implementation Status

- Other application RPCs return Unimplemented through explicit handler stubs; Temporal integration remains deferred.
- Protobuf contracts, generated code, migrations, and CI configuration are unchanged.
- Database integration execution still requires a disposable, already migrated database. Local race verification was blocked by a C compiler without 64-bit support; CI verification remains outstanding.

## [0.5.1] - 2026-11-22

PostgreSQL integration testing in CI.

### Changed

- GitHub Actions provisions a PostgreSQL 17.12 service container with a disposable `onboarding_test` database and readiness health check.
- CI sets `TEST_DATABASE_URL` with test-only credentials and applies existing migrations through Goose before running tests.
- Unit and PostgreSQL integration tests run with `go test -race -count=1 -v ./...`, disabling test-result caching and showing individual test results.
- README documents CI database setup and integration-test execution; VERSION advances to 0.5.1.

### Implementation Status

- Application code, tests, protobuf contracts, migrations, Makefile, and local environment settings are unchanged.
- Local integration tests remain opt-in through `TEST_DATABASE_URL`; CI execution requires verification in GitHub Actions.

## [0.5.0] - 2026-11-22

Application domain and repository (PR 02).

### Added

- Transport-independent Application model, application status and rejection-step types, and a constructor validating required IDs and creation time.
- Repository interface with Create, GetByID, and GetByRequestID operations.
- PostgreSQL implementation accepting the existing pgxpool helper's pool, with parameterized SQL and caller-owned connection lifecycle.
- Distinct errors for missing applications and duplicate application, request, and workflow IDs; sanitized database errors preserve context cancellation and deadline classification.
- Concise unit tests for domain validation and repository error classification.
- Opt-in PostgreSQL integration tests for nullable fields and enum round-trips, duplicate request IDs without overwriting existing data, and concurrent duplicate inserts.

### Changed

- Promoted the existing google/uuid dependency to a direct dependency.
- README documents repository behavior, explicit TEST_DATABASE_URL configuration, integration-test prerequisites, and current CI limitations.
- VERSION advances to 0.5.0.

### Implementation Status

- Create reports duplicate request IDs; GetByRequestID supports retrieving the original application. Service-level request replay and Temporal startup remain deferred.
- Protobuf contracts, migrations, handlers, services, and CI configuration are unchanged.
- Integration tests skip without TEST_DATABASE_URL; CI does not yet provision PostgreSQL or enable these tests.

## [0.4.0] - 2026-11-21

Database foundation (PR 01).

### Added

- Transactional Goose Up/Down migration for the application-owned `applications`, `terms_acceptances`, and `application_identities` tables.
- Named PostgreSQL enums with full protobuf names excluding UNSPECIFIED, unique application request/workflow IDs, per-application term uniqueness, and foreign keys with explicit NO ACTION policies.
- Reusable pgxpool connection helper with DSN validation, startup ping, cleanup on initialization failure, sanitized errors, and caller-owned pool shutdown.
- Unit tests for empty/malformed DSNs and credential redaction.
- Pinned pgx v5.7.6 dependency and Goose v3.24.3 Go tool, with explicit migration up/status/down Makefile targets.
- CI migration-file validation without a database connection.

### Changed

- Database reference records initial migration coverage, request-ID storage, enum representation, and deferred ownership/idempotency decisions.
- README documents Bash and PowerShell migration commands, explicit environment configuration, connection lifecycle, and destructive rollback behavior.
- Corrected stale README statements: account and worker already have empty main functions and are buildable placeholders.
- VERSION advances to 0.4.0.

### Implementation Status

- Services do not yet use the connection helper or run migrations automatically; API contracts and service ownership remain unchanged.
- The other five tables, repositories, business behavior, and Temporal runtime wiring remain deferred.
- Integration tests are omitted by project decision; migration execution and live database connectivity require manual verification against disposable PostgreSQL.

## [0.3.1] - 2026-11-21

Database requirements clarification.

### Changed

- Database reference now records eight tables in one shared PostgreSQL database, explicit foreign keys, uniqueness rules, and corrected relationship cardinalities.
- Documented nullable completion timestamps and review reasons, review timestamps as `timestamptz`, and account numbers as `varchar(30)`.
- Recorded application and review protobuf enums, account statuses (`ACTIVE`, `SUSPENDED`, `CLOSED`), and user roles (`CUSTOMER`, `BANKER`, `ADMIN`).
- Clarified customer matching by `id_number`, reuse of existing customer records, multiple accounts per customer, and one final review per application requiring review.
- Documented `application_id` as the Temporal workflow ID, retry and concurrency requirements, and unresolved customer identity mapping, request-ID persistence, and API documentation differences.
- Updated README to reflect the clarified database requirements; VERSION advances to 0.3.1.

### Implementation Status

- Documentation and version metadata only; runtime code, API contracts, and database schema are unchanged.
- No migrations or customer-matching implementation are included; remaining decisions are listed in `docs/AI/db.md`.

## [0.3.0] - 2026-11-20

Local development infrastructure update.

### Added

- Docker Compose configuration for PostgreSQL (`postgres:17.12`) and Temporal Dev Server (`temporalio/temporal:1.10.1`).
- Loopback-bound PostgreSQL, Temporal API, and Temporal Web UI ports, with health checks for both containers.
- Named volumes for PostgreSQL data and Temporal's embedded SQLite database.
- `.env.example` with local PostgreSQL settings and `.gitignore` excluding `.env`.

### Changed

- `make up` waits for container health checks with a 120-second timeout.
- `make logs` follows logs starting with the last 100 lines.
- README covers prerequisites, environment setup, infrastructure startup, verification, troubleshooting, and shutdown with persistent data.
- VERSION advances to 0.3.0.

### Implementation Status

- Infrastructure configuration is provided; Go services do not yet connect to PostgreSQL or Temporal.
- No application tables or database migrations are included.
- Account and worker commands and business logic remain placeholders. Temporal Dev Server is for local development.

## [0.2.1] - 2026-11-20

Documentation update for onboarding design references.

### Added

- Architecture diagram and component ownership documentation.
- Business onboarding flow and Mermaid sequences for happy-case processing and sanctions-match human review.
- Downstream retry policy distinguishing business decisions from technical failures.
- Descriptions of eight database tables and their relationships, with schema details requiring confirmation.
- Links to original system and database diagram sources under `docs/Human/`.

### Changed

- AGENTS.md documentation references now point to the available `docs/AI/` files.
- README documents the design references and distinguishes intended architecture from current implementation.

### Implementation Status

- Runtime code, API contracts, and database schema are unchanged.
- Business logic and infrastructure remain scaffolded as described in 0.2.0.
- Database documentation contains unresolved type descriptions and relationship constraints that need review before implementation.

## [0.2.0] - 2026-11-20

Scaffolding and development tooling update.

### Added

- Account domain, handler, service, repository interface, PostgreSQL repository, and test placeholders.
- Onboarding workflow, review update, activities, and application, account, third-party, and SendGrid client placeholders.
- Account and worker command placeholders and an application domain status placeholder.
- Application PostgreSQL repository and test placeholders.
- GitHub Actions CI for protobuf lint and generation consistency, Go formatting, static analysis, race-enabled tests, and builds.
- Makefile targets for generation, verification, builds, local services, and Docker Compose commands.
- AGENTS.md with project engineering and human review instructions.

### Implementation Status

- Account and worker commands have no `main` functions and cannot yet build as executables.
- New business logic, persistence, workflows, activities, clients, and tests are placeholders.
- Temporal and PostgreSQL dependencies, database migrations, and Docker Compose configuration are not yet included.
- Existing application and third-party servers continue to register unimplemented RPC handlers.

## [0.1.0] - 2026-11-14

Initial scaffold release.

### Added

- Application and third-party protobuf contracts with generated Go types and Connect RPC bindings.
- Application HTTP server on port 8080 and third-party HTTP server on port 8081, each with a health endpoint.
- Placeholder application domain, handler, repository, and service packages, plus third-party handler, service, and mock packages.
- API design documentation and Buf configuration for protobuf generation.
- README covering the project, current structure, API endpoints, and local startup instructions.
- VERSION file initialized to 0.1.0.

### Implementation Status

- Both servers register generated unimplemented RPC handlers. Business workflows, persistence, and third-party mocks remain placeholders.
